From 678faae6bbd43cd391f1ac095f4b4343f36c1607 Mon Sep 17 00:00:00 2001
From: legsmechanical <joshgaine@gmail.com>
Date: Fri, 22 May 2026 12:22:38 -0400
Subject: [PATCH] =?UTF-8?q?feat(overtake):=20co-run=20=E2=80=94=20let=20an?=
 =?UTF-8?q?=20overtake=20tool=20share=20the=20surface=20with=20a=20second?=
 =?UTF-8?q?=20UI?=
MIME-Version: 1.0
Content-Type: text/plain; charset=UTF-8
Content-Transfer-Encoding: 8bit

Adds co-run: an overtake tool can keep ticking and keep a chosen subset
of controls while a second UI (Schwung's chain editor, or Move's native
device/preset pages) uses the rest of the surface. The split is declared
by the tool as a manifest of named control groups (corun_keep_mask +
shared corun_group_for_event map), not hard-coded per tool.

- shadow_constants.h: corun_keep_mask + CORUN_GRP_* groups + shared
  event->group map + CORUN_KEEP_DEFAULT.
- schwung_shim.c: Move-native target — cable-0 MIDI filter + forward
  mirror derive cede/keep from the manifest; shadow_swap_display bypass.
- shadow_ui.c: shadow_corun_begin/end + shadow_get_corun_keep_mask;
  chain-edit + move-native target gates.
- shadow_ui.js: chain-edit target (editor renders over the tool frame,
  receives ceded input); per-control cede guards.

Proven in production by dAVEBOx (8-track sequencer) running both targets.

Co-Authored-By: Claude Opus 4.7 <noreply@anthropic.com>
